 Bi-Directional RTM for Login Feature
Requirement 1 (R1)

Requirement: User should be able to log in with a valid mobile number and password.

TC01: Verify login with valid mobile number and password.

   Forward: R1 - TC01
   Backward: TC01 - R1

TC02: Verify login with an invalid password.

   Forward: R1 - TC02
   Backward: TC02 - R1

Requirement 2 (R2)

Requirement: System should display an error message for invalid login details.

 TC03: Verify error message for invalid mobile number or password.

   Forward: R2 - TC03
 Backward: TC03 - R2

 TC04: Verify error message when login fields are left blank.

   Forward: R2 - TC04
   Backward: TC04 - R2

 Requirement 3 (R3)

Requirement: User should be redirected to the home page after successful login.

 TC05: Verify that the user is redirected to the home page after successful login.

   Forward: R3 - TC05
   Backward: TC05 - R3

 Traceability Summary

1. Forward Traceability: Requirement - Test Case
2. Backward Traceability: Test Case - Requirement
3. Bi-Directional Traceability: Requirement <-> Test Case
4. All 3 requirements are linked with the required 5 test cases.
5. This helps ensure that every requirement is covered by testing and every test case is linked to a requirement.
